#undef NDEBUG
// Review HI: the correlation miner keyed by an attribute or column other
// than concept:name, and /api/align with standard costs on nets with silent
// moves.
//
// - /api/mine's correlation miner (classic, classic_split, trace_based)
//   keyed by a typed attribute of an XES upload reads read_xes' legacy
//   objects, and keyed by a CSV column the formatted frame's cells: classic
//   reads every event's key (KeyError) and sorts the set of objects with
//   Python's list.sort (TypeError for objects Python cannot order; NaN and
//   NaT activities hold no event); classic_split sorts the objects' first
//   appearances (on a frame after dropping NaN, NaT and None rows), and a
//   NaN activity precedes and follows nothing; trace_based reads the
//   concept:name column. Labels are str() of the objects.
// - /api/align with standard costs on a discovered net reads pm4py's log
//   alignments: each trace's fitness floors its cost and its best-worst
//   cost to whole moves (a silent move costs 1), and the less-memory
//   Dijkstra prices silent moves its own way.
//
// Expected values are pm4py 2.7.22 black-box on the same inputs
// (review-harness round-hi: tc/mkhi.py, ct/cor.py, ct/al.py). Correlation
// cases where pm4py's cvxopt LP returns another plan (a tie, or a plan that
// is not optimal under its own cost matrix) are not bound.
//
// Usage: minera_server_review_hi_tests <minera_server>
